          "type": "turn",
          "question": "If a document refers to the J45 family, is that a code or a category?",
          "answer": "The term \"J45\" refers to a category in the ICD-10 coding system, specifically for asthma. In the ICD-10-CM, J45 is classified under Chapter 10, which covers diseases of the respiratory system. \n\nJ45 is not used at just three characters; it is part of a more detailed coding system that includes two independent axes related to the severity of asthma and its state at the time of the encounter. This means that when discussing J45, it encompasses a category rather than a singular code (source: \"Coding asthma: J45 and its severity and exacerbation axes\").\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
